From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Arcila <134677+tarcila@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 31 Aug 2026 12:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat(cmake): make the ANARI device library optional

The device is independent of the applications -- it exists so other ANARI
clients can capture into VSR -- but there is no way to build one without the
other. Add VSR_BUILD_ANARI_DEVICE so a build can pick either. It is forced on
for the Viskores demo, which links vsr_device directly, following how
VSR_BUILD_UI_LIBRARY handles the same situation.

Ordering the vsr subdirectory first is incidental: anari_vsr links targets
defined under it, which CMake resolves regardless, but reading it top-down is
easier when the consumer comes second.
---
 CMakeLists.txt     | 2 ++
 src/CMakeLists.txt | 4 +++-
 2 files changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index 0d63254..e5db99d 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -76,6 +76,8 @@ option(VSR_NANOVDB_USE_ZIP
   "Enable zlib so NanoVDB importer can read ZIP-compressed .nvdb files" ON)
 option(VSR_USE_LUA "Enable Lua scripting support" ON)
 
+option(VSR_BUILD_ANARI_DEVICE "Build the VSR ANARI device library" ON)
+
 if (APPLE)
   set(VSR_USE_CUDA OFF)
 else()
diff --git a/src/CMakeLists.txt b/src/CMakeLists.txt
index b2772d2..4e4f125 100644
--- a/src/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -1,8 +1,10 @@
 ## SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright (c) 2024-2026 NVIDIA CORPORATION & AFFILIATES. All rights reserved.
 ## SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
 
-add_subdirectory(anari_vsr)
 add_subdirectory(vsr)
+if (VSR_BUILD_ANARI_DEVICE)
+  add_subdirectory(anari_vsr)
+endif()
 
 # NOTE: apps must be added before tests -- tests/CMakeLists.txt gates the
 # SciVis Studio suites on `if (TARGET vsr_scivis_studio_model)`, and that
